{"body":"Five retained aliases need preparation-stage scope review. `Fe(III)-EDTA (0.66% [wt/vol] in water)` explicitly names an aqueous formulation, while four other concentration-qualified strings may denote a stock or a receiving-medium dose. The latter four are not asserted to be proven wrong solely because they contain a concentration.\n\nExact reviewed scope:\n- Finding `CH-06`; stable key `w04-independent-CH-06`; immutable peer review `20261108T070033Z-w04-successor-science-v1`.\n- `w04-chem-proposal-d-biotin-spellings`; owner `data/ingredients/mapped/Biotin.yaml`; before `26056efadc5e57f081cde6e4ce0c2e25c03530c6d564ef0df25da3bcacb59c30`; proposed SHA256 `f5e754785ccf5509bc133fb413dddba09ff6e4f1767b8997b89294bb3eaf54d9`.\n  [Exact published proposal](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Biotin.after.yaml).\n- `w04-chem-proposal-folate-b9`; owner `data/ingredients/mapped/Folic_Acid.yaml`; before `df85938271ec8f32a6d756f5213ba9661c9a7530822f333d2e02493b9f92e615`; proposed SHA256 `79b9b94956ba546897ca69172654b62bc1ff4ecd894a828da51dbe91cf4d2e2a`.\n  [Exact published proposal](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Folic_Acid.after.yaml).\n- `w04-chem-proposal-ferric-edta`; owner `data/ingredients/mapped/Fe_Iii-edta.yaml`; before `583095cb1c81bca99e71bd4be2d6d2c876b1ff8923b77820107e6968d10078a2`; proposed SHA256 `f6166de4951a66032986107f6dac307cf264b15cd555f2d935c4cd3cd22d80bc`.\n  [Exact published proposal](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Fe_Iii-edta.after.yaml).\n- `w04-chem-proposal-tungstate-malformed-alias`; owner `data/ingredients/mapped/Na2wo4_X_2_H2o.yaml`; before `b66951aba30cde0c3efe3b5ae2080a8d3445aebdffbd04b748e554f28358ffa9`; proposed SHA256 `ee4ddb16dcd7db924f74c49b55dbfb563d9da489a7a2adb9a0b03ee575a9da57`.\n  [Exact published proposal](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na2wo4_X_2_H2o.after.yaml).\n- `I1201-CHEM-P-ketoglutamate-acid-alias-rejection`; owner `data/ingredients/mapped/Alpha-ketoglutaric_Acid.yaml`; before `cc852c586e35a3ffa025ce9446da05dc235a6df8a7c0e7c2fa4c4d6ee18d371d`; proposed SHA256 `81b84944ab1121ee8c5abc5f78183d208baf1624db3844a8d0dac935a2fdca91`.\n  [Exact published proposal](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/successors/issue-1201-v1/proposals/chemistry/Alpha-ketoglutaric_Acid.after.yaml).\n\nKeep the explicit aqueous FeIII-EDTA formulation distinct from the pure-solute owner. Recover the exact original stock-versus-dose context for the other four labels before deciding whether each may resolve. Preserve text, occurrence lineage and supported new aliases. Do not create a stock from concentration text alone, infer titrant/solvent amounts, reject every parenthetical concentration, or change the native synonym policy. The already-filtered bare parenthetical solution string is outside this defect.\n\n| Owner | Exact field | Literal | Current type |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Biotin.yaml` | `synonyms/22` | `Biotin (1 μg/μL)` | `RAW_TEXT` |\n| `Folic_Acid.yaml` | `synonyms/23` | `Folic acid (5 μg/μL)` | `RAW_TEXT` |\n| `Fe_Iii-edta.yaml` | `synonyms/11` | `Fe(III)-EDTA (0.66% [wt/vol] in water)` | `RAW_TEXT` |\n| `Na2wo4_X_2_H2o.yaml` | `synonyms/2` | `Na2WO4 x 2 H2O (0.1% w/v)` | `HYDRATE_FORM` |\n| `Alpha-ketoglutaric_Acid.yaml` | `synonyms/6` | `alpha-ketoglutaric acid (100 mM).` | `RAW_TEXT` |\n\nThe exact field/value hashes, original source tags and complete occurrence-evidence pointers are preserved in `ACTIONABLE-MATRIX.json` CH-06. The listed proposal links expose the retained literals; no supplier page is being presented as proof of a source recipe’s stock stage.\n\nDeduplication: #1189 tracks four different W10 owners and is not exact coverage for these five literals. #1201 may track resulting source completion; it does not establish stock identity. No matching stock/owner tracker was found in the captured all-state bodies and relevant indexed search/comments.\n\nReview context: W04 published head `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9`, frozen campaign base `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`. Main as observed at `0dac278466699129a083343a921c2e0ca18a9ab4` has the same eighteen affected inherited-owner blobs as the frozen baseline; this is not a report of already-applied campaign curation. The full independent assembly covers 188 source cases and 115 proposals and remains `needs_curation`. Original peer review and evidence are immutable. Agent-authored new mapping evidence must satisfy #1226 without relabeling historical human evidence. The fix must use existing native guarded proposal validation and independent re-review; it grants no maintained-owner or export approval and requires no new gate, threshold, or synonym-selection rule.\n\n<!-- mim-review-round:20261108T071043Z-w04-final-scientific-issue-plan -->\n<!-- mim-review-bundle:concentration-alias-scope -->\n<!-- mim-fingerprints:w04-independent-CH-06 -->\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHc_lQ","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Reviewed W05 head `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d`, frozen base `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`. The preserved external review is `20261108T071144Z-worker08-independent-worker05-full188-payload138`, YAML SHA256 `bdde7d4101546e0e43f0752e4587c4d0c3a0fb43f887d82eee2d869edd5c06b0`. All 188 case-decision hashes and all 138 selected payload hashes were independently rebound to the published core; the sealed scientific review remains needs_curation. This comment records bounded follow-up before author correction, not approval or application.\n\nExact W05-CR-F08 extension to #1230. These four concentration-qualified owner families require original stock-versus-dose scope. Concentration text alone does not establish a solvent, complete stock or wrong identity. Preserve all literal/history provenance and supported current source deltas; unresolved preparation remains withheld.\n\n| Owner | Exact field | Literal/type | Native MIM / Claw eligible |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Riboflavin.yaml` | `synonyms/27` | `Riboflavin (0.2 mg/ml)` / `RAW_TEXT` | True / True |\n| `Riboflavin.yaml` | `synonyms/29` | `Riboflavin (0.05 μg/mL)` / `RAW_TEXT` | True / True |\n| `Hepes.yaml` | `synonyms/12` | `HEPES (10mM)` / `RAW_TEXT` | True / True |\n| `Ki.yaml` | `synonyms/6` | `KI (0.01% w/v)` / `RAW_TEXT` | True / True |\n| `Fe_Iii_Citrate.yaml` | `synonyms/14` | `Ferric citrate (0.1%, w/v)` / `RAW_TEXT` | True / True |\n\nNative eligibility is a pinned function probe, not a new consumer-index rebuild or scientific support. Exact payload/preimage and source pointers are retained in W05 findings.json and the coordinator scope-and-policy-verification.json.  Preserve all original captures, history, known source/form/role and supported-versus-withheld holds. Use existing guarded proposal validation and independent review; no new code, test, schema, threshold, owner-selection rule, merge, corpus publication or approval transfer is authorized by this finding.\n\n<!-- mim-fingerprints:w05-external-w05-cr-f08 -->\n","createdAt":"2026-11-08T07:23:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1230#issuecomment-6718701461","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":1230,"state":"OPEN","title":"Separate explicit stock and unresolved concentration aliases from pure-solute identity","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1230"}
